-- 030: richer bios, why lines, genres, festivals, labels and city for pack 1 (artists 1-10). Text fields only. Only fills when the pack is longer or the field is empty. No em dashes, no personal-life details, no unverified links or stats.
update public.artists a set
  bio = case when length(v.bio) > length(coalesce(a.bio,'')) then v.bio else a.bio end,
  why = case when length(v.why) > length(coalesce(a.why,'')) then v.why else a.why end,
  genres = case when coalesce(array_length(a.genres,1),0) < array_length(v.g,1) then v.g else a.genres end,
  festivals = case when coalesce(array_length(a.festivals,1),0) < array_length(v.f,1) then v.f else a.festivals end,
  labels = case when coalesce(a.labels,'')='' and v.lab<>'' then v.lab else a.labels end,
  based_city = case when v.city<>'' and coalesce(a.based_city,'') in ('','India','USA') then v.city else a.based_city end
from (values
($q$indo-warehouse$q$,$q$Indo Warehouse is a record label and experiential series founded by Kunal Merchant and Kahani (Armaan Gupta) that showcases the beauty of South Asian culture, music, and rhythm within the global language of electronic music. They coined the genre "Indo House", fusing deep techno beats with South Asian classical influences. In just three years, they moved from intimate New York clubs to sold-out international venues across Europe, Asia, and the Middle East. Their performances feature up to 25 performers including musicians, vocalists, and dancers. Historic Coachella 2025 debut as first South Asian electronic collective. Performed at Hï Ibiza, F1 Singapore, DGTL, Magnetic Fields, and Lollapalooza.$q$,$q$First South Asian electronic collective at Coachella (2025, both weekends). Created "Indo House" genre. Historic debut at Gobi stage with Rohit Bal couture tributes and diasporic sound. Most globally visible Indian electronic act in 2025-2026.$q$,array[$q$Indo House$q$,$q$Melodic Techno$q$,$q$Deep House$q$,$q$South Asian Electronic$q$]::text[],array[$q$Coachella 2025$q$,$q$Hï Ibiza$q$,$q$F1 Singapore$q$,$q$DGTL$q$,$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$Lollapalooza$q$]::text[],$q$Indo Warehouse Records$q$,$q$New York, USA$q$),
($q$nikki-nair$q$,$q$Nikki Nair is an Atlanta, Georgia-based producer and DJ of Indian-American heritage who has become one of the most booked Indian-origin electronic artists in the global underground. His productions merge electro, leftfield techno, breaks, bass, and ghettotech into colourful, twisted dancefloor hybrids. He is known for bombastic, unexpected DJ sets that refuse genre boundaries, flipping between ghettotech, UKG, experimental disco, and beyond. Formerly based in Knoxville, Tennessee, he moved to Atlanta during the pandemic and left his day job in December 2022 to focus on music full-time. He launched his own label "n goes to infinity" in 2022, focused on releases between underground club music and American-style bass music. In 2023, he released the mini-album "Set the Roof" with his personal hero Hudson Mohawke. Named one of Mixmag's top 25 artists to watch and one of DJ Mag's 12 artists you need to listen to in 2022. Championed by Crack Magazine as one of the artists who defined 2023.$q$,$q$Most booked Indian-origin producer in global underground. Historic Boiler Room Hyderabad set (2022) featuring Stefflon Don and Sidhu Moose Wala samples. Boiler Room Berlin b2b Hudson Mohawke. Currently on active 2026 world tour with dates across Europe and North America. Named in Crack Magazine's artists who defined 2023.$q$,array[$q$Breakbeat$q$,$q$Electro$q$,$q$Techno$q$,$q$Bass$q$,$q$Leftfield$q$,$q$Ghettotech$q$,$q$UKG$q$]::text[],array[$q$Nuits Sonores$q$,$q$Boiler Room Hyderabad$q$,$q$Boiler Room Berlin$q$,$q$Glastonbury$q$,$q$Bang Face$q$,$q$Bass Coast Festival$q$,$q$Dirtybird Campout$q$,$q$World Renowned$q$]::text[],$q$n goes to infinity, Dirtybird, Scuffed, Lobster Theremin, Pretty Weird, Studio Barnhus, Refuge Worldwide$q$,$q$Atlanta, Georgia, USA$q$),
($q$kohra$q$,$q$Kohra (Madhav Shorey) is a New Delhi-based electronic music producer and DJ, founder of Qilla Records (established 2011). "Kohra" means "fog or mist" in Urdu; "Qilla" means "fort or castle." A rock and metal drummer turned DJ, his travels and time studying at Swinburne University in Melbourne stoked his desire to create a homegrown scene for Delhi. He got his start as part of India's first widely recognized live electronica band, Jalebee Cartel. Through Qilla, he helped bring international attention to Indian underground dance music. His productions have appeared on Sol Selectas, Traum, Parquet, Steyoyoke, Motek, Blindfold, Tulipa, and Particles, many hitting Beatport Top 100 in over 4 genres. Tale of Us, Sam Paginini, Nick Warren, Joran Van Pol, Roy RosenfelD, Township Rebellion, Xenia Beliayeva, JSPR, and Atish have supported Qilla releases. He has shared stages with Pete Tong, Deadmau5, Dubfire, Richie Hawtin, Adam Beyer, Chris Liebing, Josh Wink, Patrice Baumel, Joseph Capriati, and Oliver Huntemann. In 2020, he released his debut album "akhõ", a 10-track LP paying homage to 17th-century mystic poet Kabir, blending ambient and progressive textures with breaks, electro, and jungle. John Digweed played half of it during his Bedrock Bunker Session. In 2024, Qilla celebrated its 100th release with the compilation "Chakravyūh" (spinning wheel in Sanskrit). 35 tracks of hypnotic techno and breaks, first Qilla release on vinyl, featuring pan-Asian artists. In 2024, launched "Sacred Alchemy" club nights at antiSOCIAL Mumbai and Beats Per Minute Hyderabad. Announced plans for 4 vinyl releases per year and revival of Alchemy festival.$q$,$q$Most Boiler Room appearances by an Indian solo electronic artist (Delhi NCR June 2024, Bengaluru Aug 2024). Built India's most respected underground electronic label from scratch. Took Indian techno global through Qilla Records. His debut album akhõ was played by John Digweed. Qilla 100th release "Chakravyūh" was a landmark moment for Indian electronic music.$q$,array[$q$Techno$q$,$q$Deep House$q$,$q$Ambient$q$,$q$Experimental$q$,$q$Hypnotic Techno$q$,$q$Progressive$q$,$q$Breaks$q$,$q$Electro$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$Echoes of Earth$q$,$q$Amsterdam Dance Event$q$,$q$DGTL$q$,$q$Boiler Room Delhi NCR$q$,$q$Boiler Room Bengaluru$q$,$q$Boxout Weekender$q$,$q$Goat Fest$q$,$q$EDC$q$,$q$Awakenings India$q$]::text[],$q$Qilla Records, Traum Schallplatten, Trapez, Manual Music, Sudbeat, Sol Selectas, Parquet, Steyoyoke, Motek$q$,$q$New Delhi$q$),
($q$sheral$q$,$q$Sheral is a Delhi-based DJ and graphic designer who moves through house, bass, breaks, footwork, and techno to shape a sound that is distinctly hers. She is a rising female DJ in the Indian electronic scene, known for her colourful energy and explorative approach. She made her Boiler Room debut in Gurugram (Delhi NCR) in June 2024 alongside Kohra, Prismer, Girls Night Out, and AK Sports. In April 2026, she returned to Boiler Room for a Mumbai double-header, recorded on April 10, 2026, a night that promised relentless energy across the lineup. Active in the Magnetic Fields and DGTL circuit. Also a graphic designer by profession, bringing visual sensibility to her artistic identity.$q$,$q$Rising female DJ in Indian electronic scene. Boiler Room Delhi NCR 2024 debut. Returned to Boiler Room Mumbai in April 2026, latest verified Boiler Room appearance. Part of India's new wave of underground electronic artists. Graphic designer bringing visual-artistic crossover.$q$,array[$q$House$q$,$q$Bass$q$,$q$Breaks$q$,$q$Footwork$q$,$q$Techno$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$DGTL$q$,$q$Boiler Room Delhi NCR$q$,$q$Boiler Room Mumbai$q$]::text[],$q$$q$,$q$New Delhi$q$),
($q$prismer$q$,$q$Rohan Kalé, hailing from New Delhi, India, creates explorative, bass-driven electronic music under his pseudonyms 'Prismer' and 'Don Jiro.' He was exposed to electronic music in 2010, London, UK during his formative years and has been a Producer/DJ ever since. His sound is an all-encompassing mix taking heavy influences from techno to jungle, house to dubstep, breakbeat to disco and everything in between. With his first few releases signed to Boxout.FM (IN), Reel Long Overdub (UK), Tokyo Hell (JP) etc, that have been on heavy rotation on BBC 6 Music, NTS, Keep Hush etc, he has earned his mark as one of India's brightest artists of recent times. He has shared the stage with DJ Stingray, Benjamin Damage, Denham Audio, Pangaea, Fixate, TommyFourSeven, Ivy Lab, Champion, and Rider Shafique. Performed at prestigious events like Magnetic Fields Festival, Bass Camp Festival, Levi's Music Week, Grasslands Festival (Nepal), Bira91 Festival, and Boiler Room Delhi NCR (June 2024). In October 2025, he was part of The Warehouse Project India debut, a historic three-city takeover across Bengaluru, Mumbai, and Hyderabad. His set from Mumbai was recorded and released as "The Warehouse Project India: Prismer in Mumbai, Oct 26, 2025" on Apple Music. He is also the founder of "Mixed Feelings", a party series in Delhi creating safe spaces for marginalized communities, launched post-pandemic. In February 2026, he performed at Magnimusik Selections 03 in Delhi.$q$,$q$Emerging Indian electronic producer on world stage. Boiler Room Delhi NCR 2024. The Warehouse Project India debut October 2025, historic Manchester clubbing institution's first India tour. Multiple international label releases (Boxout.FM, Reel Long Overdub, Tokyo Hell). BBC 6 Music, NTS, Keep Hush rotation. Creator of "Mixed Feelings" safe space party series in Delhi. One of India's brightest artists according to Resident Advisor.$q$,array[$q$Techno$q$,$q$Bass$q$,$q$Jungle$q$,$q$House$q$,$q$Dubstep$q$,$q$Breakbeat$q$,$q$Disco$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$Bass Camp Festival$q$,$q$Levi's Music Week$q$,$q$Grasslands Festival$q$,$q$Bira91 Festival$q$,$q$Boiler Room Delhi NCR$q$,$q$The Warehouse Project India$q$]::text[],$q$Boxout.FM, Reel Long Overdub, Tokyo Hell$q$,$q$New Delhi$q$),
($q$girls-night-out$q$,$q$Girls Night Out is an Indian electronic DJ collective pushing India's electronic sound forward. The collective performed at the historic Boiler Room Delhi NCR broadcast on June 8, 2024, alongside Kohra, Sheral, Prismer, and AK Sports, a landmark moment for Indian electronic music on the global platform. In February 2026, they were confirmed on the lineup for Magnetic Fields Nomads at Abheygarh Palace in Khetri, Rajasthan, performing from 10:30 PM to 12:30 AM. The collective represents the new generation of Indian electronic acts breaking into global platforms, with a focus on inclusive, community-driven dancefloor experiences. Active in the Magnetic Fields and DGTL circuit.$q$,$q$Collective pushing India's electronic sound forward. Boiler Room Delhi NCR June 2024, historic Indian electronic showcase. Magnetic Fields Nomads 2026 confirmed (Feb 13-15, Khetri, Rajasthan) with scheduled set time 10:30 PM - 12:30 AM. Part of India's new wave of underground electronic artists focused on inclusive dancefloor experiences.$q$,array[$q$Electronic$q$,$q$House$q$,$q$Techno$q$,$q$Club$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields Nomads 2026$q$,$q$Boiler Room Delhi NCR$q$,$q$DGTL$q$]::text[],$q$$q$,$q$New Delhi$q$),
($q$ak-sports$q$,$q$AK SPORTS is an Indian electronic DJ/producer delivering high NRG sets spanning hard techno, 160+ BPM, and all things hard, fast & fun. A respected DJ/Producer, radio host (Rinse FM), and label head. Performed at Boiler Room Delhi NCR in June 2024 alongside Kohra, Sheral, Prismer, and Girls Night Out. Also performed at Boiler Room Bengaluru in August 2024. Part of the new generation of Indian electronic acts breaking into global platforms.$q$,$q$New generation of Indian electronic acts breaking into global platforms. Multiple Boiler Room appearances (Delhi NCR 2024, Bengaluru 2024). Rinse FM radio host.$q$,array[$q$Hard Techno$q$,$q$Techno$q$,$q$Electronic$q$,$q$Hardcore$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$Boiler Room Delhi NCR$q$,$q$Boiler Room Bengaluru$q$]::text[],$q$$q$,$q$$q$),
($q$midnight-traffic$q$,$q$Midnight Traffic is a Hyderabad-based electronic duo and techno visionary, creating hypnotic soundscapes with modern design, deep elements, and pulsating rhythms. Active in the Hyderabad electronic scene and regional scene builders. Performed at Boiler Room Hyderabad in May 2022 alongside Nikki Nair, Suchi, and Murthovic. Part of Qilla Records collective. Featured on Qilla's Chakravyūh compilation (2024) with track "Mantis." In April 2026, performed on Japanese streaming platform DOMMUNE's BROAD.J series (BROAD.J 3536), gaining international exposure for Hyderabad techno.$q$,$q$Active Hyderabad electronic duo, regional scene builders. Boiler Room Hyderabad 2022. Qilla Records artist. Featured on Chakravyūh compilation. DOMMUNE Japan exposure April 2026.$q$,array[$q$Techno$q$,$q$House$q$,$q$Electronic$q$,$q$Hypnotic Techno$q$]::text[],array[$q$Krunk events$q$,$q$Boiler Room Hyderabad$q$,$q$DGTL$q$]::text[],$q$Qilla Records$q$,$q$Hyderabad$q$),
($q$suchi$q$,$q$SUCHI is a DJ and producer with Indian and Norwegian heritage whose formative raving experiences in Oslo, London and New York underpin an intentionally global-inspired club vision. Her distinct sound is best experienced in dynamic sets infused with house, percussion, bass, and techno with a flair for the experimental. Named one of the top 25 artists to watch by Mixmag and one of the 12 artists you need to listen to in 2022 by DJ Mag. Championed by Pitchfork, Vogue, Rolling Stone, Wired, and Electronic Beats. In 2025, she launched her own imprint Ikke Sant (Norwegian for "isn't that right?"). The debut release, Sub Cut EP, delivers three tracks of psychedelic, hypnotic club music. Support from Ben UFO, Pearson Sound, Midland, Pariah, Or:la, Ciel, Florentino, DJ JM, Peder Mannerfelt, HAAi, and Bradley Zero. Noted appearances at Fabric, Phonox, Warehouse Project, Glastonbury, By:Larm, Sonar Festival, Waterworks, Magnetic Fields and ADE. Two landmark broadcasts for Boiler Room (India tour with Parris and Nikki Nair). Australian tour supporting Jon Hopkins. Recorded mixes for DJ Mag, NTS Radio, BBC Radio 6 and HÖR. In 2026, performing at Cadavra in City Center on June 6, 2026.$q$,$q$Early Indian electronic artist to get Boiler Room platform (Hyderabad 2022). Global club circuit regular (Fabric, Glastonbury, Sonar). Launched Ikke Sant label in 2025. Named top 25 by Mixmag and top 12 by DJ Mag 2022. Indian-Norwegian heritage creating unique global club sound.$q$,array[$q$House$q$,$q$Techno$q$,$q$Bass$q$,$q$Percussion$q$,$q$Experimental$q$,$q$Leftfield$q$]::text[],array[$q$Boiler Room Hyderabad$q$,$q$Fabric$q$,$q$Glastonbury$q$,$q$Sonar Festival$q$,$q$By:Larm$q$,$q$Waterworks$q$,$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$ADE$q$,$q$Warehouse Project$q$,$q$Lost Village$q$,$q$Field Day$q$]::text[],$q$Ikke Sant, Ghostly International/Spectral Sound, !K7, Coastal Haze, Boxout.FM$q$,$q$Manchester, UK$q$),
($q$murthovic$q$,$q$Murthovic (MSR Murthy) is a DJ, producer, sound practitioner and researcher with close to 20 years in the electronic music field. He is part of India's original Boiler Room class (Hyderabad 2022) and a Magnetic Fields regular. He is the co-creator of "Elsewhere In India", a pioneering transmedia project with visual artist Thiruda (Avinash Kumar) that combines game engine technology with live performance, creating immersive experiences where cultural heritage meets cutting-edge technology. The project features digital human avatars of Murthovic and Thiruda, and takes place in a futuristic 2079 setting. In 2026, their latest project "Jal, Jungle, Zameen" debuted at Magnetic Fields Nomads (Feb 13-15, Khetri, Rajasthan), a 60-minute live electronica performance excavating Indian ecological heritage through sound, visuals and digital environments. The performance converged with Rajasthan's living musical traditions, featuring hereditary musicians Gopika, Sawai, Jakir, Dilip, and Roshan on instruments such as kamaycha, morchang, bhapang, khartal, and dholak. In March 2026, Elsewhere In India is set for a one-night Melbourne show at The Indian Sun. Also performed audiovisual Bharatnatyam DJ sets in Hyderabad (2023).$q$,$q$Part of India's original Boiler Room class (Hyderabad 2022). Magnetic Fields regular. Innovative transmedia project "Elsewhere In India" with Thiruda, pioneering Indian audio-visual performance. "Jal, Jungle, Zameen" at Nomads 2026 featuring Rajasthan hereditary musicians. Melbourne show March 2026. 20 years in electronic music.$q$,array[$q$Electronic$q$,$q$Live Electronica$q$,$q$Transmedia$q$,$q$Techno$q$,$q$Carnatic-Electronic$q$,$q$Bass$q$,$q$House$q$]::text[],array[$q$Magnetic Fields$q$,$q$Magnetic Fields Nomads$q$,$q$Boiler Room Hyderabad$q$,$q$Ars Electronica$q$,$q$British Council India$q$,$q$Science Gallery London$q$]::text[],$q$Qilla Records$q$,$q$Hyderabad$q$)
) as v(slug,bio,why,g,f,lab,city) where a.slug=v.slug;
